\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.  Hushed was the evening hymn,\cf0 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 The temple courts were dark,
\par The lamp was burning dim
\par Before the sacred ark,
\par When suddenly a voice Divine
\par Rang through the silence of the shrine.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  The old man, meek and mild,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 The priest of Israel, slept;
\par His watch the temple child,
\par The little Levite, kept;
\par And what from Eli's sense was sealed
\par The Lord to Hannah's son revealed.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  O give me Samuel's ear,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 The open ear, O Lord,
\par Alive and quick to hear
\par Each whisper of  Thy word,
\par Like him to answer at Thy call,
\par And to obey Thee first of all.
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 
\par \pard\fi-270\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  4.  O give me Samuel's heart,
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 A lowly heart, that waits
\par Where in Thy house Thou art,
\par Or watches at Thy gates
\par  By day and night - a heart that still
\par  Moves at the breathing of Thy will.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  5.  O give me Samuel's mind,
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 A sweet unmurmuring faith,
\par Obedient and resigned
\par To Thee in life and death,
\par That I may read, with childlike eyes,
\par \pard      Truths that are hidden from the wise.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

